In May 2020, Rose announced she would be leaving the series ahead of its second season;<ref name="RoseLeave" /> while it was initially announced that it was mutually decided between Rose, the studio, and the network for her to leave,<ref name="TVLineRoseDeparture">{{Cite web |last=Ausiello |first=Michael |date=May 20, 2020 |title=Ruby Rose's Batwoman Exit: The Story Behind Her Shocking Departure |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/ruby-rose-batwoman-season-2-departure-scoop-1199899/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200521072644/https://tvline.com/2020/05/20/ruby-rose-batwoman-season-2-departure-scoop/ |archive-date=May 21, 2020 |access-date=May 21, 2020 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref><ref name="VarietyRoseDeparture">{{Cite web |last=Otterson |first=Joe |date=May 20, 2020 |title=Why 'Batwoman' Star Ruby Rose Left the CW Series |url=https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/batwoman-ruby-rose-exit-1234612077/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200521235024/https://variety.com/2020/tv/news/batwoman-ruby-rose-exit-1234612077/ |archive-date=May 21, 2020 |access-date=May 21, 2020 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Rose's ''Batwoman'' co-star Camrus Johnson confirmed in October 2021 that Rose had in fact been fired after "multiple complaints" about her on-set behavior.<ref name="RoseFired">{{Cite web |last=Ortiz |first=Andi |date=October 21, 2021 |title={{'}}''Batwoman''{{'}} Co-Star Camrus Johnson Says Ruby Rose Was Definitely Fired |url=https://www.thewrap.com/batwoman-camrus-johnson-response-ruby-rose |website=[[The Wrap]] |access-date=October 21, 2021 }}</ref> The producers reaffirmed their commitment to the series and finding a new actress who is gay to lead future seasons.<ref name="RoseLeave">{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=May 19, 2020 |title=Ruby Rose Exits the CW's 'Batwoman', DC Series To Recast Iconic Lead Role For Season 2 |url=https://deadline.com/2020/05/ruby-rose-exits-batwoman-dc-the-cw-series-to-recast-iconic-lead-role-season-2-shocker-shakeup-1202938863/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200520032555/https://deadline.com/2020/05/ruby-rose-exits-batwoman-dc-the-cw-series-to-recast-iconic-lead-role-season-2-shocker-shakeup-1202938863/ |archive-date=May 20, 2020 |access-date=May 19, 2020 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> Rose later called being the lead of a series "taxing" and stated her back surgery following an on-set accident in 2019 was a contributing factor in deciding to leave, saying it was "time for me to take a break to fully heal and then return" to acting. Spending time in isolation because of the COVID-19 pandemic also allowed Rose "to just think about a lot of different things and what you want to achieve in life and what you want to do," which allowed her "a great opportunity to have a dialogue about a lot of things" with the producers.<ref name="RoseEWAug2020">{{Cite magazine |last=Cordero |first=Rosy |date=August 11, 2020 |title=Ruby Rose explains how the pandemic played a role in her decision to leave Batwoman |url=https://ew.com/tv/ruby-rose-explains-decision-leave-batwoman/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200814130034/https://ew.com/tv/ruby-rose-explains-decision-leave-batwoman/ |archive-date=August 14, 2020 |access-date=August 11, 2020 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref>

The following month, a casting notice for a new character named Ryan Wilder was revealed, indicating the series was looking to replace Kane as Batwoman.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Zalben |first=Alex |date=June 2, 2020 |title='Batwoman' Season 2 To Replace Ruby Rose's Kate Kane With A New Character |url=https://decider.com/2020/06/02/batwoman-season-2-ryan-wilder-replace-kate-kane-batwoman/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603054132/https://decider.com/2020/06/02/batwoman-season-2-ryan-wilder-replace-kate-kane-batwoman/ |archive-date=June 3, 2020 |access-date=June 3, 2020 |website=Decider}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=June 2, 2020 |title='Batwoman': Title Character to Have New Identity Following Ruby Rose's Exit |url=https://deadline.com/2020/06/batwoman-new-lead-character-identity-ruby-rose-exit-replacement-recasting-1202949699/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603015921/https://deadline.com/2020/06/batwoman-new-lead-character-identity-ruby-rose-exit-replacement-recasting-1202949699/ |archive-date=June 3, 2020 |access-date=June 2, 2020 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> Dries defended the decision to introduce a new character as Batwoman, asserting that the series would continue to "respect everything that Ruby put into the Kate Kane character."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Andreeva |first=Nellie |date=June 6, 2020 |title='Batwoman' Showrunner On Introducing New Character Instead Of Recasting Following Ruby Rose's Exit – ATX |url=https://deadline.com/2020/06/batwoman-showrunner-recast-ruby-rose-exit-introducing-new-character-ryan-wilder-atx-1202952981/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200607102115/https://deadline.com/2020/06/batwoman-showrunner-recast-ruby-rose-exit-introducing-new-character-ryan-wilder-atx-1202952981/ |archive-date=June 7, 2020 |access-date=June 8, 2020 |website=[[Deadline Hollywood]]}}</ref> She also revealed Kane would not be killed, and her disappearance would be a key story-line during season two.<ref>{{Cite magazine |last=Agard |first=Chancellor |date=June 10, 2020 |title=Batwoman boss reveals Kate Kane won't be killed off: 'We'll never erase her' |url=https://ew.com/tv/batwoman-boss-clarifies-comments-about-kate-kanes-fate/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200612105018/https://ew.com/tv/batwoman-boss-clarifies-comments-about-kate-kanes-fate/ |archive-date=June 12, 2020 |access-date=June 10, 2020 |magazine=[[Entertainment Weekly]]}}</ref>

Matt Webb Mitovitch at ''[[TVLine]]'' and Jill Pantozzi of ''[[io9]]'' both felt replacing Kane as Batwoman would be a detriment to the series. Mitovitch felt it would "create more problems than it solves", saying it would take away from the established character dynamics (namely the "central" one between Kate and Alice) and the various plot threads waiting to be resolved from the end of the [[Batwoman (season 1)|first season]]. He added: "a simple if momentarily awkward recast would have kept all established storylines and dynamics intact; Season 2 could then pick up where the solid Season 1 left off. Instead, loyal viewers will be asked to re-invest in something that is significantly new, while also possibly giving up some of the things they liked most about the show."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovitch |first=Matt Webb |date=June 3, 2020 |title=Batwoman's Plan to Not Simply Recast Kate But Introduce a New Lead Character Has More Cons Than Pros |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/batwoman-season-2-kate-kane-gone-new-character-added-2888040/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603174825/https://tvline.com/2020/06/03/batwoman-season-2-kate-kane-gone-new-character-added/ |archive-date=June 3, 2020 |access-date=June 3, 2020 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref> Pantozzi felt the series could have approached the casting of a new lead actress more creatively, given the series exists in "a universe of time travel, doppelgängers, and literal face-swapping". She concluded, "if they are truly doing away with the Kate character it feels like a bizarre move. Fans could much easier come to terms with a simple replacement actress, than having to go through a convoluted story of why a random lesbian has taken up the cowl so soon after Kate did. ... It seems like a lot of explaining to do when there's a much easier option."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pantozzi |first=Jill |date=June 3, 2020 |title=Batwoman's Idea to Replace Ruby Rose Is Curiously Boring for a Comic Show |url=https://www.gizmodo.com.au/2020/06/batwomans-idea-to-replace-ruby-rose-is-curiously-boring-for-a-comic-show/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200609060147/https://www.gizmodo.com.au/2020/06/batwomans-idea-to-replace-ruby-rose-is-curiously-boring-for-a-comic-show/ |archive-date=June 9, 2020 |access-date=June 3, 2020 |website=gizmodo}}</ref> Conversely, ''[[Collider (website)|Collider]]''{{'}}s Liz Shannon Miller felt a new character was "the right call" and "a big swing" for the series. Miller pointed to the "long-established precedent" in the comics of new characters taking over mantles from others. Like Mitovitch, Miller questioned what the new character would mean for the series' supporting cast, since their connections to Kate were "their primary reason for being a part of the show's storyline". She also hoped "Ryan Wilder" was a place-holder name, "because the trend of naming strong female characters with traditionally male names has just gotten tired at this point".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Miller |first=Liz Shannon |date=June 3, 2020 |title=Why a New Character Playing 'Batwoman' Might Be the Right Call |url=https://collider.com/batwoman-ruby-rose-replacement-new-character-ryan-wilder/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200603233801/https://collider.com/batwoman-ruby-rose-replacement-new-character-ryan-wilder/ |archive-date=June 3, 2020 |access-date=June 3, 2020 |website=[[Collider (website)|Collider]]}}</ref>

In early July 2020, [[Javicia Leslie]] was cast as Ryan Wilder, the new Batwoman.<ref name="LeslieCast">{{Cite web |last=Ausiello |first=Michael |date=July 8, 2020 |title=''Batwoman'' Taps Javicia Leslie to Replace Ruby Rose in Title Role |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/javicia-leslie-new-batwoman-season-2-ruby-rose-recast-2899456/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200730134653/https://tvline.com/2020/07/08/javicia-leslie-new-batwoman-season-2-ruby-rose-recast/ |archive-date=July 30, 2020 |access-date=July 8, 2020 |website=TVLine}}</ref> Rose was supportive of Leslie's casting.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Nemetz |first=Dave |date=July 8, 2020 |title=Ex-Batwoman Star Ruby Rose Reacts to Javicia Leslie Taking Over Lead Role |url=https://www.tvline.com/news/batwoman-ruby-rose-javicia-leslie-recast-reaction-season-2-2899537/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210227211929/https://tvline.com/2020/07/08/batwoman-ruby-rose-javicia-leslie-recast-reaction-season-2/ |archive-date=February 27, 2021 |access-date=July 8, 2020 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref><ref name="RoseEWAug2020" /> [[Wallis Day]] was later cast as Kate Kane where it was claimed that she surgically altered her appearance.<ref name=dm21 /> Rose, commenting on an Instagram tribute to her time in the role, stated that she was "stoked" about Day's casting.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Mitovitch |first=Matt Webb |date=March 22, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose on Batwoman's Kate Kane Recast: 'I Am Stoked' for Wallis Day |url=https://www.tvline.com/casting-news/ruby-rose-batwoman-kate-kane-recast-reaction-wallis-day-1234653066/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210323005236/https://tvline.com/2021/03/22/ruby-rose-batwoman-kate-kane-recast-reaction-wallis-day/ |archive-date=March 23, 2021 |access-date=March 22, 2021 |website=[[TVLine]]}}</ref>

In an interview with ''ComicBookMovie.com'' when asked if she would reprise Kate at some point, Rose said, "I would totally do it. I don't think it would serve the story because I think building the new Batwoman is more important than going back too far into Kate Kane, but of course I would." Then she added on "I've watched a couple of episodes, and I think how they're handling it is beautiful. I think it's [Ryan Wilder's] time to shine."<ref>{{Cite web |last=Conlin |first=Dan |date=March 13, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose Says She Might Return To Batwoman, But There's A Catch |url=https://gamerant.com/ruby-rose-batwoman-return-possible/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210313193543/https://gamerant.com/ruby-rose-batwoman-return-possible/ |archive-date=March 13, 2021 |access-date=March 14, 2021 |website=Game Rant}}</ref> However, in later in October 2021, after Rose spoke out about alleged abuse and neglect on set, she walked back on the statement, saying she would not return for "any amount of money nor if there were a gun to my head".<ref name="toxic">{{Cite magazine |date=October 20, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose Alleges Gruesome Injuries, Toxic Behavior on 'Batwoman' Set |url=https://www.rollingstone.com/tv/tv-news/ruby-rose-batwoman-set-injuries-allegations-1244881/ |url-status=live |magazine=Rolling Stone |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020142647/https://www.rollingstone.com/tv/tv-news/ruby-rose-batwoman-set-injuries-allegations-1244881/ |archive-date=October 20, 2021 |access-date=October 20, 2021}}</ref>

=== Filming ===
Production on the pilot episode began on March 4 and concluded on March 25, 2019, in [[Vancouver, British Columbia]].<ref name="PilotProductionDates" /><ref name="PilotFilming" /> Additional filming took place in [[Chicago, Illinois]].<ref name="ChicagoFilming" /> Filming for the rest of the season began on July 4 and was set to conclude in mid-2020.<ref name="S1ProductionDates" /> On March 12, 2020, Warner Bros. Television shut down production on the series due to the [[COVID-19 pandemic]].<ref name="Productionshutdown" /> Filming for the second season began on September 3, 2020,<ref>{{Cite web |last=Jenna Anderson |title=Batwoman Stars Begin Production on Season 2 in New Video |url=https://comicbook.com/tv-shows/news/batwoman-spoilers-season-2-filming-production-cast-video/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200904033223/https://comicbook.com/tv-shows/amp/news/batwoman-spoilers-season-2-filming-production-cast-video/ |archive-date=September 4, 2020 |access-date=September 4, 2020 |website=comicbook.com|date=September 3, 2020 }}</ref> and concluded on May 10, 2021.<ref name="S2Filming">{{Cite news |date=August 21, 2020 |title=DGC BC Production List |work=[[Directors Guild of Canada]] |url=https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Documents/Production-List.pdf |url-status=live |access-date=August 21, 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200821200823/https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Documents/Production-List.pdf |archive-date=August 21, 2020}}</ref> Filming for the third season began on July 19, 2021, and concluded on December 22.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 8, 2021 |title=DGC BC Production List |url=https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211008184419/https://www.dgc.ca/assets/Uploads/BritishColumbia/AvailsProductionLists/Production/Production-List.pdf |archive-date=October 8, 2021 |access-date=December 25, 2021 |website=[[Directors Guild of Canada]]}}</ref>

===Controversy===
In 2019, Rose suffered an injury during stunt work on the series. She spoke about the experience being close to "severing my spinal chord (sic). I was in chronic pain and yet couldn't feel my arms". She required emergency surgery.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Bennett |first=Anita |date=September 29, 2019 |title='Batwoman' Star Ruby Rose Undergoes Emergency Surgery After Stunt Injury Left Her Facing Paralysis |url=https://deadline.com/2019/09/batwoman-star-ruby-rose-undergoes-emergency-surgery-after-stunt-injury-left-her-facing-paralysis-1202747538/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211021102349/https://deadline.com/2019/09/batwoman-star-ruby-rose-undergoes-emergency-surgery-after-stunt-injury-left-her-facing-paralysis-1202747538/ |archive-date=October 21, 2021 |access-date=October 21, 2021}}</ref> In 2020, Amanda Smith, a production assistant working on the show, was paralyzed following a bucket lift being lowered onto her head. Warner Bros. Television stated they cooperated with an investigation into onset safety.<ref>{{Cite web |last1=Nellie Andreeva |last2=Denise Petski |date=March 16, 2020 |title='Batwoman' Production Assistant Paralyzed In On-Set Accident, Warner Bros. TV Cooperating With Investigation |url=https://deadline.com/2020/03/batwoman-production-assistant-paralyzed-on-set-accident-amanda-smith-warner-bros-tv-invesigation-1202884231/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211021102348/https://deadline.com/2020/03/batwoman-production-assistant-paralyzed-on-set-accident-amanda-smith-warner-bros-tv-invesigation-1202884231/ |archive-date=October 21, 2021 |access-date=October 21, 2021}}</ref>

In October 2021, Rose spoke out on the working conditions of her time on ''Batwoman''. She alleged that after her spine injury, she was forced back to work with the implications from studio executives being that the entire crew would lose their jobs if she did not. She also stated that production was rushed and corners cut during the [[COVID-19 pandemic in the United States|COVID-19 pandemic]] and that there were many [[Stunt performer|stuntpersons]]' injuries on-set as well as her own, including one which she said cast and crew should have received therapy for afterward.<ref name="toxic" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Earl |first=William |date=October 20, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose Alleges Misconduct and Unsafe Conditions on 'Batwoman' Led to Exit |url=https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/ruby-rose-batwoman-injuries-1235093470/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020235725/https://variety.com/2021/tv/news/ruby-rose-batwoman-injuries-1235093470/ |archive-date=October 20, 2021 |access-date=October 21, 2021 |website=[[Variety (magazine)|Variety]]}}</ref> Rose spoke out against co-stars [[Dougray Scott]] and Camrus Johnson's behavior on-set, calling the former abusive and the latter an "egomaniac kid who worked one day a week". Scott responded that these allegations are "entirely made-up",<ref>{{Cite web |title='Batwoman' Alum Dougray Scott Denies Ruby Rose's 'Entirely Made Up' Accusations He Abused Women |url=https://www.thewrap.com/batwoman-dougray-scott-denies-ruby-rose-abuse-accusations/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211021102347/https://www.thewrap.com/batwoman-dougray-scott-denies-ruby-rose-abuse-accusations/ |archive-date=October 21, 2021 |access-date=October 21, 2021 |website=The Wrap|date=October 20, 2021 }}</ref> while Johnson stated Rose was fired and he felt "we have a lot of great souls working on this show".<ref>{{Cite tweet |number=1451034556996390914 |user=CamrusJ |title=Batfam ya know I couldn't go the whole day without saying something! I love y'all, don't think I haven't seen all the love today. But yea fam, she was fired. And it is VERY hard to be fired when you're the lead. Imagine what u have to do for that 2 happen |date=October 21, 2021 |access-date=December 19, 2021}}</ref>

In a statement, Warner Bros. Television dismissed the allegations by Rose and said that her contract was not picked up for season two because of multiple complaints about her workplace behavior.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Porter |first=Rick |date=October 20, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose Says They Were Fired From 'Batwoman' |url=https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/ruby-rose-fired-batwoman-1235034072/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211020162239/https://www.hollywoodreporter.com/tv/tv-news/ruby-rose-fired-batwoman-1235034072/ |archive-date=October 20, 2021 |access-date=October 20, 2021 |website=[[The Hollywood Reporter]]}}</ref> This was expanded on when a production assistant, Alexander J. Baxter, came forward to confirm Rose had been fired from the show for alleged "dictator"-like behaviour.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Tassi |first=Paul |title='Batwoman' PA Reveals Why Ruby Rose Was Actually Fired, Countering Her Story |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2021/10/24/batwoman-pa-reveals-why-ruby-rose-was-actually-fired-countering-her-story/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220430022512/https://www.forbes.com/sites/paultassi/2021/10/24/batwoman-pa-reveals-why-ruby-rose-was-actually-fired-countering-her-story/ |archive-date=April 30, 2022 |access-date=October 25, 2021 |website=Forbes}}</ref> However, Rose disputed these claims and produced emails, texts and other evidence on her concerns with the working conditions and ethics on set.<ref>{{Cite web |date=October 24, 2021 |title=Ruby Rose Releases Emails to Back Up Her Batwoman Allegations |url=https://screenrant.com/batwoman-ruby-rose-allegations-emails-evidence/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20211025160533/https://screenrant.com/batwoman-ruby-rose-allegations-emails-evidence/ |archive-date=October 25, 2021 |access-date=October 25, 2021 |website=Screen Rant}}</ref>

== Release ==
=== Broadcast ===
The series debuted on The CW October 6, 2019.<ref name="SeriesPremiereDate" /> In New Zealand, the series is streamed on [[TVNZ]]'s free streaming service [[TVNZ OnDemand]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=TVNZ Highlights: 5–11 October |url=https://www.tvnz.co.nz/what-to-watch/news-feed/tvnz-highlights--5-11-october |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200522080843/https://www.tvnz.co.nz/what-to-watch/news-feed/tvnz-highlights--5-11-october |archive-date=May 22, 2020 |access-date=November 23, 2019 |publisher=[[TVNZ OnDemand]]}}</ref> In the United Kingdom, the series is shown on [[E4 (TV channel)|E4]].<ref>{{Cite web |last=Pritchard |first=Tom |date=January 14, 2020 |title=Batwoman and Harley Quinn are Coming to E4 in the UK |url=https://www.gizmodo.co.uk/2020/01/batwoman-harley-quinn-e4-uk/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200331155010/https://www.gizmodo.co.uk/2020/01/batwoman-harley-quinn-e4-uk/ |archive-date=March 31, 2020 |access-date=March 31, 2020 |website=[[Gizmodo]] UK}}</ref> In Canada, it is aired on [[Showcase (Canadian TV channel)|Showcase]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Batwoman:Peak TV Canada |url=https://peaktv.ca/show/batwoman/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210124094405/https://peaktv.ca/show/batwoman/ |archive-date=January 24, 2021 |access-date=January 16, 2021 |website=Peak TV}}</ref>

=== Home media ===
Season 1 was released on [[DVD]] and [[Blu-ray]] on August 18, 2020. Special features included deleted scenes, a gag reel, highlights from DCTV's 2019 [[San Diego Comic-Con]] panels, and a behind-the-scenes featurette entitled "On the Set". The release also included a bonus disc with all five episodes of the "[[Crisis on Infinite Earths (Arrowverse)|Crisis on Infinite Earths]]" crossover event.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Latchem |first=John |date=April 30, 2020 |title='Batwoman' Season One on Disc Aug. 18 |url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/batwoman-season-one-on-disc-aug-18/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200524213634/https://www.mediaplaynews.com/batwoman-season-one-on-disc-aug-18/ |archive-date=May 24, 2020 |access-date=April 30, 2020 |website=Media Play News}}</ref>

Season 2 was released on DVD and Blu-ray on September 21, 2021. Special features included deleted scenes, a gag reel, and two featurettes entitled "Villains Analyzed" and "Never Alone: Heroes and Allies".<ref>{{Cite web |last=Latchem |first=John |date=June 23, 2021 |title='Batwoman' Season One on Disc Sept. 21 |url=https://www.mediaplaynews.com/batwoman-season-two-on-disc-sept-21/ |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20210711002140/https://www.mediaplaynews.com/batwoman-season-two-on-disc-sept-21/ |archive-date=July 11, 2021 |access-date=July 10, 2021 |website=Media Play News}}</ref>

Season 3 was released on Blu-ray & DVD on July 12, 2022. Special features included deleted scenes and a gag reel.<ref>{{cite web | url=https://www.aussieosbourne.com/2022/05/batwoman-third-and-final-season-on-disc.html | title="Batwoman: The Third and Final Season" on Disc July 12 | access-date=May 6, 2022 | archive-date=May 23, 2022 | archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220523014402/https://www.aussieosbourne.com/2022/05/batwoman-third-and-final-season-on-disc.html | url-status=live }}</ref>

